<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Kumu Device Spec

Type-level device contract for kumu devices. Derives from pranala edges.
''Spec layer only — no runtime dispatch overhead.'' Runtime derives bindings from the same
pranala tiddler edges via `extractReactionBindings`.

''No separate registration step.'' Adding a kumu type means authoring a type meme with
`reaction:listenable` and `reaction:subscribable` edges. The spec derives at parse time.

''Verse alignment:'' A kumu device meme is a Lararium `creative_device` equivalent.
`@editable` properties = ahu slot URIs. OUTPUT pins = `KumuListenable`. INPUT pins = `KumuSubscribable`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/verse-model>>

!! Verse 5.6+ Device Model

UEFN Verse 5.6+ uses single-inheritance class composition:

```verse
my_device := class(creative_device):
    @editable
    OnActivated : listenable(agent) = barrier_device.IsActivatedEvent

    @editable
    TargetUri : string = ""

    Enable(Agent : agent) : void = ...
```

Lararium maps this directly:

| Verse | Lararium |
|---|---|
| `class(creative_device)` | `control:extends` edge → `KumuDeviceSpec.extendsType` |
| `class(P, I, J)` composition | worn components (`control:has` edges) → `KumuDeviceSpec.componentTypes` |
| `listenable(T)` field | `KumuListenable` (`verseKind: "listenable"`) |
| `event(T)` field | `KumuListenable` (`verseKind: "event"`) |
| public input method | `KumuSubscribable` |
| `@editable` property | ahu slot URI in `KumuDeviceSpec.slots` |
| DEB editor wire | `papalohe` pranala edge (instance-level `ReactionBinding`) |
| `Await(event)<suspends>` | `ReactionGraph.subscribeOnce()` (kukali primitive) |
| `using { /Path }` | module namespace import — NOT trait composition |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/exports>>

!! Exports

!!! `KumuListenable` — OUTPUT event pin

```
name         — event name (e.g. "OnActivated", "OnDamaged", "OnReset")
description? — human description
verseKind?   — "listenable" (awaitable + subscribable) | "event" (signalable + awaitable only)
payloadType? — Verse type string (e.g. "agent", "int"); absent = void
```

`verseKind` distinguishes:
* ''`listenable`'' — engine-vended; supports `Subscribe()` (persistent multi-consumer). The common case for built-in UEFN device events.
* ''`event`'' — user-instantiated (`event(T){}`); supports `Await()` + `Signal()` only. No `Subscribe()`. Fire-once semantics.

When absent: treat as `"listenable"`.

Declared via `reaction:listenable` pranala edges on the kumu type meme.

---

!!! `KumuSubscribable` — INPUT function pin

```
name         — handler name (e.g. "Enable", "Disable", "SetDamage")
description? — human description
payloadType? — Verse parameter type matching the connected listenable's payload
effects?     — Verse effect specifiers as string array (e.g. ["suspends"], ["decides", "transacts"])
```

''`effects` field:'' Space-separated Verse specifiers stored as metadata. Not interpreted in TS — available for canvas authoring tools and code generation. Verse semantics:
* `suspends` — function may yield the calling fiber; analogous to TypeScript `async`
* `decides` — function participates in branch/race/rush resolution
* `transacts` — function participates in atomic transaction grouping

Declared via `reaction:subscribable` pranala edges on the kumu type meme.

---

!!! `KumuDeviceSpec` — type-level device description

Derives from the type meme's pranala edge list, not from a TS class hierarchy.

```
typeUri          — canonical type URI (no fragment)
listenables      — OUTPUT pins (reaction:listenable edges)
subscribables    — INPUT pins (reaction:subscribable edges)
slots            — ahu slot URIs (@editable analogue; caller supplies)
extendsType?     — single parent class URI (control:extends edge; Verse single inheritance)
componentTypes   — worn component URIs (control:has edges; Verse class(...) composition, no privileged is-a parent)
```

''Three semantic layers — do not conflate:''

# ''Ahu-slot tree'' (document structure) — `fragment-parent` + `slot` tiddler fields. One `.md` decomposes into root + N slot fragment tiddlers. NOT a pranala edge.

# ''`control:extends`'' (one edge) — the single Verse parent class. `my_device := class(creative_device)` → one edge, `toUri = creative_device URI`. Maps to `extendsType`.

# ''`control:has`'' (N edges) — Verse class(...) composition as worn components. Maps to `componentTypes`. N edges allowed.

---

!!! `KumuInstanceRef` — runtime instance address

```
typeUri       — type meme URI
nameFragment  — user-selected friendly name (human label)
uuidFragment  — crypto.randomUUID() stable wiring address
```

Both fragments produce tiddler title URIs:
```
lar:///type-path#/nameFragment   — human-readable wiki-local label
lar:///type-path#/uuidFragment   — stable UUID address for papalohe wiring
```

!!! `kumuInstanceUris(ref) → { named, uuid }`

Derives both tiddler URIs from a `KumuInstanceRef`.

---

!!! `kumuDeviceSpecFromEdges(typeUri, edges, slots?) → KumuDeviceSpec`

Derives a `KumuDeviceSpec` from a flat edge list (pass `parseMemeEdges(typeUri, text)` directly).

Selection rules:
* `reaction:listenable` edges with `fromUri === typeUri` → `listenables`
* `reaction:subscribable` edges with `fromUri === typeUri` → `subscribables`
* `control:extends` edge → `extendsType`
* `control:implements` edges → `implementsTypes`
* Roles `observes`, `throttles`, `debounces` — not reflected in spec (future: modifier semantics)

<<!/ahu>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/reaction-engine-removal>>

!! ReactionEngine Removal

`ReactionEngine` (TS class, inline dispatch) was removed in the yin-collapse sprint (2026-05-15).

The dispatch surface it owned collapsed into:
* `reaction-router.ts` TW5 startup module — nalu-driven dispatch (production path)
* `ReactionGraph` in `reaction-graph.ts` — routing table and test dispatch surface

No TS overlay engine runs beside TW5. The wiki IS the engine. The nalu IS the tick.
See: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu#/yin-collapse-law`

<<!/ahu>>

<<~/ahu>>

